# DI-first (uie-iv / pyiv)

Default path is **[`uie-iv`](../../crates/uie-iv/README.md)** (Guice / [pyiv](https://github.com/rl337/pyiv) style).
New shared services, loader chains, and CI vs live wiring go through **`Module` +
`Binder` + `Injector`**, not scattered `if live` or raw `UIE_*` env checks.

- Register bindings in `Module::install` (`AcceptanceEnvModule`, `ServeEnvModule`, test overrides).
- Consume via [`uie_acceptance::composition`](../../crates/uie-acceptance/src/composition.rs) or an explicit `Injector::from_modules`.
- Do **not** add string registries, service locators, or duplicate static graphs outside `uie-iv`.
- Domain crates (`uie-core`, modality engines, IPC) stay **injector-agnostic**; only composition roots import `uie-iv`.
- Tests force CI/live with `OverrideCiModule` / `OverrideLiveModule`, not by flipping env mid-test.
- Injectables **own** their config (paths, URLs, credentials). Do not grow ambient global settings bags.

Normative detail: [`docs/requirements/dependency-injection.md`](../../docs/requirements/dependency-injection.md).
Workflow: [`.cursor/skills/di-config-ownership/SKILL.md`](../skills/di-config-ownership/SKILL.md).

```rust
// BAD — call-site env branch
if std::env::var("UIE_ACCEPTANCE_MODE").unwrap_or_default() == "live" { ... }

// GOOD — injected profile
if injector().acceptance_profile().skip_live_test("live_us_009") {
    return;
}

// GOOD — test override, no env
let inj = Injector::from_modules(&[&OverrideCiModule]).unwrap();
```